From d9726429cf0b1655e513a1530ed10ad714437934 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aman <rockndrap@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:32:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] terminal: add terminal.tab_title setting for shell-set
 titles

Task terminal tabs are titled after the task label, and other tabs after
the running process, so long-lived TUIs that name themselves via OSC 2
(agent CLIs, for example) are indistinguishable across tabs. Their title
is already captured in Terminal::breadcrumb_text for the breadcrumb bar.

Add terminal.tab_title, defaulting to the existing behavior, with a
shell_title mode that prefers the shell-set title when there is one.
Renamed tabs keep their custom title in both modes.
