 The title can be set by your shell using the escape sequence `\e]2;Title\007`.
 
+### Tab Title
+
+By default a terminal tab is titled after the task that spawned it, or after the running
+process and its directory. Set `tab_title` to `shell_title` to use the title the shell or
+program sets via the escape sequence above instead, which is useful for long-lived TUIs
+that name themselves:
+
+```json [settings]
+{
+  "terminal": {
+    "tab_title": "shell_title"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Tabs fall back to the default title until a title has been set, and a tab renamed with
+{#action terminal::RenameTerminal} always keeps its custom name.
+
